    "capture": "Private append-only anonymous Unix slabs retain immutable UTF-8 slices under Rc. The existing consuming join unmaps source slabs after their last slice retires instead of leaving malloc medium-region pages resident. Small fragments, insufficient headroom and mapping failure retain the ordinary heap path; non-Unix targets use heap storage. Directory replacement, offsets and unfinished tail backing are funded before choosing an optional slab, so the slab cannot crowd out the rest of that fragment.",
    "accounting": "Every real slab and owner header is reserved on the existing managed memory account before physical allocation. Optional admission previews the same cumulative work ledger without spending on a declined preference; failed physical allocation remains charged once. No ledger renewal, per-operation protocol, new resource route or secondary executor.",
