    "histogram_banks": "The general ASCII one/two-grapheme histogram lowering uses four disjoint counter banks after128/16,384 logical cells have at least eight starts each. Admission reserves every physical counter plus worst-case Entry/key backing before entry, checks local/global headroom, and retains serial storage on short input, tight headroom or a lost shared reservation race. Existing finite work bounds cover zeroing, counting, reduction and materialization; no per-start callbacks, extra permission protocol or new resource authority.",
    "immutable_text_fact": "One same-entry fixed weak frozen-storage identity caches ASCII-without-CRLF, never source payloads or permissions. Admission includes the inline slot plus complete weak Arc shell (144B on this target,1152 work units); replacement drops the old weak token first. Every invocation still pays the existing complete scan-work bound and validates source kind, genuine owner, geometry and finite limits. New entry/round state reacquires facts. Work policy37 rejects old36 receipts; ABI12 and typed IR27 are unchanged.",
    "native_host_features": "canonical-native-resources reuses the original artifact admission, capability preview/revalidation, provider/schema checks and transaction pipeline without enabling resident-routing in deployed native hosts. Resident routing depends on that SAME shared feature; the build/test frontend retains resident APIs. No copied authority, new executor, changed artifact wire format, relaxed safety check or release-profile change. Route introspection reports None when no resident execution support exists."
